    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0811" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860h.9111 RR/7–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 462<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Yugoslavia </hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">plain</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-11">July 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. …</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Borba</hi> sharply criticizes Reuters for attitude of
                    “protectionism” and “inclination contrary to fact” in favor of Greeks during
                    Yugoslav-Greek dispute on treatment of Macedonians in north Greece. Editorialist
                    denies charge of Reuters editor that Yugoslavia wishes to make territorial
                    claims on Greece and hence press campaign by pointing out alleged expansionist
                    ambitions of Greek chauvinist officials. He admits that Yugoslavs and “all true
                    democrats” are <pb facs="0812" n="680" xml:id="pg680"/> against Athens
                    Government and that Yugoslavia hopes question of Greek misrule in Macedonia will
                    be subject of “international forum” if not Big Three Conference.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
